  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWhile investigating #11505 I found a separate issue:\n\nIn https://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/14226 there are some different behaviors:\n\n* Per spec, as far as I can tell, the focus order should be: 1, first image first rect, first image second rect, 2, second image first rect, second image second rect, 3.\n* Safari, Chrome: first image first rect, first image second rect, 1, 2, 3\n* Firefox: 1, both images first rect, both images second rect, 3. (Tabbing backwards reaches the \"2\" link but gets stuck in a loop, unable to reach the \"1\" link again.)\n\nThe spec's model is not implemented. WebKit and Chromium seems to just use the DOM order of the `area` elements and show only focus rings for the first image, which seems simple.",
